NEARS-3527 — Regression sweep: store_id scoping + pre-existing modules.required /
name-uniqueness validation, unaffected by this ticket's fix.

=== store_id scoping (cross-store) ===
Logged in as ts@ts.com (store_id=35). role id=1 belongs to store_id=19 (a
different vendor's role, pre-existing fixture).

GET /vendor-panel/custom-role/edit/1
-> HTTP 500 (Illuminate\View\ViewException, "Trying to access array offset on
   null" in vendor-views/custom-role/edit.blade.php)
-> No role name/modules from store 19 leaked in the response body.
-> Backend log (production.ERROR, [FAIL], see excerpt below) confirms the
   controller's existing scope
   `EmployeeRole::where('store_id',Helpers::get_store_id())->where(['id'=>$id])->first(...)`
   returned null (correctly excluded, since store_id 19 != 35) and the BLADE
   (not this ticket's code) then dereferences $role['name'] unconditionally.

  [2026-09-13 04:59:47] production.ERROR: [FAIL] Trying to access array offset
  on null (View: .../vendor-views/custom-role/edit.blade.php)
  {"trace_id":"208ed614a6d55b271575cc8113a7a4c8",
   "correlation_id":"90a619a6-691e-4d16-87a2-28da611ec496",
   "type":"Illuminate\\View\\ViewException",
   "endpoint":"/vendor-panel/custom-role/edit/1"}

POST /vendor-panel/custom-role/update/1 (name[]=HACKED-CROSS-STORE, modules[]=order)
-> HTTP 419 (no CSRF token could be scraped from the 500 page above)
-> DB: SELECT * FROM employee_roles WHERE id=1; -> UNCHANGED
   (name still "QA Manager A", store_id still 19, modules still ["order","item"])

VERDICT on the substantive regression check ("a vendor cannot touch another
store's custom role via this endpoint"): PASS — store_id scoping is intact,
zero leak, zero mutation. The 500-vs-clean-404 UI/error-surface quality gap is
PRE-EXISTING (the `edit()` method's null-handling is untouched by this
ticket's diff — the diff touches only store()/update()'s validation rules)
and is filed separately as a regression_bug, non-blocking for this ticket.

=== modules.required (empty array) — store() ===
POST /vendor-panel/custom-role/create, name[]=QA-Empty-Modules, NO modules[] field
-> HTTP 302 back to create form
-> toastr.error('Please select atleast one module')
-> Behavior unchanged from pre-fix (this rule already existed;
   Rule::in() is additive on top of it, never replacing it).

=== name uniqueness (scoped by store_id) — store() ===
POST /vendor-panel/custom-role/create, name[]=QA-Pos-Store-27-Updated (already
taken by role id=10, same store), modules[]=order
-> HTTP 302 back to create form
-> toastr.error('The name has already been taken.')  (Laravel's default unique
   message — store()'s custom $messages array has no name.unique override,
   unlike update()'s; this is pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket)
-> DB: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM employee_roles WHERE name='QA-Pos-Store-27-Updated';
   -> 1 (no duplicate created)

